#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# partial_fractions

#% text
# `partial_fractions(f, x)` gives the partial fraction decomposition of the rational function f in x over the complex numbers.

#% text
# `partial_fractions(f, x, extension: reals)` keeps the irreducible real quadratic factors of the denominator.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For a denominator with simple roots a the terms are `residue/(x - a)`, the residue being numerator(a)/denominator'(a), plus the polynomial part. Repeated roots, or roots `solve` cannot give, fall back to the rational decomposition of `apart`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
partial_fractions(1/(x^2 - 1), x)
#% output
#= -1/(2*(1 + x)) + 1/(2*(-1 + x))

#% cell
partial_fractions(1/(x^2 + 1), x)
#% output
#= -im/2/(-im + x) + im/2/(im + x)

#% cell
partial_fractions((19 + 5*x + x^2)/(12 + 4*x + 3*x^2 + x^3), x, extension: reals)
#% output
#= 5/(4 + x^2) + (3 + x)^-1

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `apart`, `together`, `solve`
